e vertex sends that much more than it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON "},{"code":"NetworkSimplex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", OR-Tools"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SimpleMinCostFlow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX "},{"code":"min_cost_flow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the opposite sign), or nil when there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none: the supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, then, for each edge in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, "},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", before any work. Which optimum is returned when several"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exist is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCostFlow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"supp